    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="10.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 10.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="292" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe hine ofer þæne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.19"/> dæg healde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.20"/>, agyfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.21"/> hine þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> bisceope<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.22"/> ⁊ forgylde hine XI siðan ⁊ ðam cingce CXX scyll'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="292" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se þe hine ofer þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.3"/> dæg healde, agife hine þam biscope ⁊ forgilde hine endlifan syþan ⁊ þam cyninge twa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.5"/> hundred ⁊ twentig scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="292" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.18"/> sine licentia supertenebit eum, reddat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.19-2"/> episcopo et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.4"/> undecies persoluat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.20-2"/> et regi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.21-2"/> CXX solid'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="293" ed="#liebermann"/>Et quicumque illum ulterius . ., reddat illum episcopo, persoluatque illum undecies, et regi CXX solidos.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="164" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ se þe hine ofer þæne dæg healde agyfe hine þam bisceope ⁊ forgylde hine XI siðan ⁊ ðam cingce CXX<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#ICn_10-1.robnote.fn.5"/> scyll'.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="242" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And se ðe hine ofer þæne dæg healde, agyfe hine þam bisceope and forgylde hine XI siðan and ðam cingce CXX scyllinga.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="293" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.de.1"/> wer sie über diesen Tag hinaus vorenthält, zahle sie dem Bischof und vergelte sie [ihm] elffach<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.de.2"/>, und dem König 120 (220<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_10-1.lnote.de.3"/> <hi rend="italic">A</hi>) Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever withholds it beyond that day, let him pay it to the bishop and pay it [to him] elevenfold, and the king 120 (220, A) shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_10-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="165" ed="#robertson"/>And he who withholds them beyond that date shall give them up to the bishop, and repeat the payment eleven times, and [pay] 120 shillings to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="243" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And anyone who withholds it beyond that day shall give the money to the bishop, and do so again eleven times over, and one hundred twenty shillings to the king.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="293"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_11-1">VIII Atr 11.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 11, 1</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_11-1">VIII Atr 11.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 10:1: (HomN LXI) VIII Atr 11:1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">In G, ‘healde’ was added after ‘dæg’ but marked for deletion. Liebermann compares VIII Atr 11.1.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 293, October 2026 (MS Cons); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 242 / 243, October 2026 (was “cxx”, now “CXX”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">CXX scyllinga: twa hundred and twentig scillinga A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þone <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þone Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">healde <hi rend="italic">fügt zu aber unterpunctirt G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">healde added by G, but dotted for deletion</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">agife <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">agife Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biscop ⁊ forgild h. endlifan syþan ⁊ ð. cyning 220 scill. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biscop ⁊ forgild h. endlifan syþan ⁊ ð. cyning 220 scill. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et qui <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et qui Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.19-2" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-atur <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-atur K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et persoluantur r. quinquaginta [<hi rend="italic">auch Hn.</hi> 11, 4] <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et persoluantur r. quinquaginta [also Hn. 11, 4] K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.21-2" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">.h. [autem?] <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">.h. [autem?] added by Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">293</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> retinuerit</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply retinuerit</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 6, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">see above 6, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">willkürlich in</hi> 9, 1 <hi rend="italic">und</hi> 10, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">arbitrarily in 9, 1 and 10, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 11, 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 11, 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nur formell anderer Ausdruck für 12fach in VIII Atr 11, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Only formally a different expression for twelvefold in VIII Atr 11, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_10-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wie <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 9, 1¹.—Die ‘50’ Schilling in Q²⁰ und Hn sind richtig aus 120 zu ¹/₄₈ £ in Normannische von ¹/₂₀ £ umgerechnet; Inst meint wieder (<hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. 3, 2⁸), Cnut rechne nach dem Schilling von ¹/₆₀ £</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">As <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 9, 1¹. — The ‘50’ shillings in Q²⁰ and Hn are correctly converted from 120 of ¹/₄₈ £ into Norman shillings of ¹/₂₀ £; Inst again supposes (<hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 3, 2⁸) that Cnut reckons by the shilling of ¹/₆₀ £</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_10-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. Hn. 11, 4.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_10-1.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><label>cxx</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">twa hundred</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">twentig scill'</hi> A; 220 <hi rend="italic">scill.</hi> Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
